  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U4L-READ-1",
      "paper": "review",
      "title": "The Magic Show",
      "text": "Last month, our science club had a big discussion about a school show. My favorite subject is science, so I joined right away. We wanted a fun idea, no matter how hard it was. Sam, who is good at magic, said he could be the magician. He kept his plan a secret, like a code. On the show day, we were all in good shape. Sam used a sharp knife to cut an apple and then divided the pieces among the crowd. The apples were smooth, not rough. Suddenly, a real rabbit appeared on the table! We had to feed it and keep it alive backstage. After the show, many students looked for us to say thank you. That night I had a sore throat from shouting, but I did not care. We still hear from those happy students today."
    }
  ],
